  "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2{X}_{1}-{X}_{2}-3{X}_{3}] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-1)^{2}\\cdot 2+(-3)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =16+2+9-4-24+18 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
